WEBVTT

00:08:59.758 --> 00:09:01.211
but also her personal genome.

00:09:01.235 --> 00:09:02.445
And it looks really good.

00:09:02.469 --> 00:09:05.065
Then she challenges all
her competitors to do the same.

00:09:05.089 --> 00:09:07.024
Do you think that's not going to happen?

00:09:07.048 --> 00:09:09.282
Do you think it would have
helped John McCain?

00:09:09.306 --> 00:09:11.099
(Laughter)

00:09:11.123 --> 00:09:14.341
How many people in the audience
have the last name Resnick, like me?

00:09:14.365 --> 00:09:15.523
Raise your hand.

00:09:15.547 --> 00:09:16.720
Anybody? Nobody.

00:09:17.175 --> 00:09:18.620
Typically, there's one or two.

00:09:18.644 --> 00:09:21.197
So my father's father
was one of 10 Resnick brothers.

00:09:21.221 --> 00:09:25.306
They all hated each other, and all moved
to different parts of the planet.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.249
So it's likely I'm related
to every Resnick that I ever meet,

00:09:28.273 --> 00:09:29.424
but I don't know.

00:09:29.448 --> 00:09:32.485
So imagine if my genome
were De-identified, sitting in software,